<title>JAPAN: Sakura Bank says appoints Okada as new president.</title>
<headline>Sakura Bank says appoints Okada as new president.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sakura Bank Ltd said on Friday that it would promote executive director Akishige Okada to president on June 1, succeeding Shunsaku Hashimoto, who will become an adviser.</p>
<p>Sakura, one of the top 10 commercial banks in Japan, also named another executive director of the bank, Masahiro Takasaki, as the new chairman, replacing Kenichi Suematsu.</p>
<p>Suematsu will also become an adviser on June 1.</p>
</text>
